import { useGrokTheme, Image, useEffect, useRef, useState, type CSSProperties, type PointerEvent, type ReactNode } from "grok/canvas";

/**
 * Pinned .me pack — billboard.
 * Link-tree column: avatar, name, handle, bio, full-width Install tiles, link chips, footer.
 * Header is those four fields only — no pack wordmark, no kicker.
 * Tiles and chips are a liqui lens (displacement + frost + specular + tint).
 * Avatar and icons stay solid. The whole tile is the install link.
 * A trailing emoji run on the display name sits beside the hero at half size.
 * Long names, dense chips, and blank fields stay inside the column for any owner.
 * Type is one see-through face: silver at 0.82 on a dark device, near-solid
 * graphite on a light device, plus the now-playing legibility shadow. Dark
 * still shows the field through the strokes. Day is dense enough to read on
 * paper. Same face for the handle, the bio, and the footer.
 * The display name uses the tile ink: the greyer see-through face of the
 * titles, descriptions, and chips, so the silk shows through the same way.
 * No forced uppercase, no wide tracking.
 * The display name is those letterforms only — no pane, tile, or pill behind it.
 * Weight and size carry the hierarchy: name, then handle, then bio.
 * Tiles and chips lift, wash, and press. The rim is one rounded rect: a crisp
 * specular lip and a clearer body, not a second corner stroke.
 * Graphite plus silver is an animated lumen field: slow blooms and a drifting sheen.
 * The glass edge comes from blooms, diagonal bands, and the scrim. Those blooms stay neutral.
 * Color, or any named accent, replaces that field with photoreal liquid-silk plates
 * (teal folds, a cyan ribbon, a peach drop). Silver on color keeps the plates' own palette.
 * A named accent hue-shifts the silk. Day keys those plates onto a paper base.
 * Dark keeps the studio plates. Both follow the device. Not lacquer.
 * The page ground is that same stage base, full-bleed on all four sides:
 * day paper, dark charcoal, graphite the device field. On a desktop the silk
 * meets the viewport edges. The install column stays the red-line measure,
 * centered, with silk in the side margins. A phone keeps the full-width
 * column and its safe-area inset. Viewport, host peek, and overscroll meet
 * the field. Theme white is not a frame around it.
 * Link chips are monochrome site icons. The handle stays on the accessible
 * name, not as a word in the glass.
 * No hairline grid.
 * APPEARANCE is not a setup lock. The page follows the opener's device
 * (host light is day, host dark is the charcoal field). A baked night, dark,
 * or day is ignored. Night is not a deeper mode.
 * STAGE is graphite or color (unset stays graphite).
 * ACCENT is silver, rose, sage, violet, amber, or teal (unset stays silver).
 * A named accent hue-shifts the silk field only. Tiles and chips stay the neutral glass.
 * The focus ring may take a quiet accent stroke. Silver leaves graphite on
 * the device base.
 * No photographed frost plates.
 * Replace the constants and the bots/links arrays. Leave the JSX alone. See README.md.
 *
 * Optics adapted from liqui (MIT), leefanv/liqui-design:
 * packages/glass/src/LiquiGlass.tsx, filterRegistry.ts, glass.css, tokens.ts
 * apps/www/registry/liqui/ui/button.tsx
 * apps/www/registry/liqui/components/media-player/player-backdrop.tsx
 * apps/www/registry/liqui/components/media-player/now-playing.tsx
 */

